<title>CHILE: Entel leads Chile Dec telephone traffic.</title>
<headline>Entel leads Chile Dec telephone traffic.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Entel was top carrier in Chile's highly competitive multicarrier telephone service in December with the firm carrying 33 percent of international and 42 percent of national long-distance calls, said official figures.</p>
<p>The following are figures for market share in the national and international long-distance markets in December. Company</p>
<p>		 National	 International</p>
<p> Entel	   41.98	    33.26</p>
<p> CTC Mundo     30.71	    20.83</p>
<p> Chilesat	16.95	    16.32</p>
<p> VTR		4.30	    12.20</p>
<p> BellSouth	1.67	    10.03</p>
<p> Transam	  1.66	     3.08</p>
<p> CNT Carrier    2.50	     0.65</p>
<p> Iusatel	  0.23	     3.63</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
